Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:45:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] fix: return 503 + Retry-After when the LLM provider
 rate-limits, not a 500

Integration finding #12: a second /scene/ask within the minute failed on Groq's 429 ("output
tokens per minute limit 1000") and reached the headset as HTTP 500. A 429 means "try again
shortly": one app-level handler for openai.RateLimitError now answers 503 with Retry-After (the
provider's value rounded up to whole seconds, else 60) on every route that reaches an LLM
(/scene/ask, /agent/command, /voice/command). The app already shows 503 as "needs the live
model". api.md documents it and the vision output cap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
